{"id":"80","title":"Health and Medicine Vocabulary","goal":"Name selected body parts, symptoms, professionals, and care-related terms to describe a concern and ask a question.","language":"en","study":[{"id":"80-study-0","title":"Start here","blocks":[{"id":"ch80-b0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"You do not need a diagnosis to explain what hurts. Choose the words for the concern you need to report; use the other groups as a reference."}],"span":[6,6],"phraseIds":[]}],"line":6,"ja":"","theme":"health-vocabulary"},{"id":"80-visual","title":"Look & understand","widget":"body","blocks":[]},{"id":"80-study-1","title":"Body parts","blocks":[{"id":"ch80-b1","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Head, ears, neck, shoulders, chest, back, arms, hands, hips, legs, knees, ankles, and feet","emphasis":true},{"text":" name common locations. The "},{"text":"elbow","emphasis":true},{"text":" is the joint in the middle of an arm; the "},{"text":"forearm","emphasis":true},{"text":" is between elbow and wrist; the "},{"text":"wrist","emphasis":true},{"text":" joins the hand to the arm. "},{"text":"Fingers","emphasis":true},{"text":" are on hands; "},{"text":"toes","emphasis":true},{"text":" are on feet. The "},{"text":"thigh","emphasis":true},{"text":" is the upper leg; the "},{"text":"calf","emphasis":true},{"text":" is the back of the lower leg; the "},{"text":"shin","emphasis":true},{"text":" is its front; the "},{"text":"heel","emphasis":true},{"text":" is the back of the foot. An "},{"text":"armpit","emphasis":true},{"text":" is under the arm where it joins the body."}],"span":[10,10],"phraseIds":["ch80-p263324456941496","ch80-p163127433727868","ch80-p30659324900187","ch80-p120596790187310","ch80-p3351912737377","ch80-p23619361059318","ch80-p65721800097752","ch80-p126658544794755","ch80-p35632778760348","ch80-p161295954255530","ch80-p214058024729802"]},{"id":"ch80-b2","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Abdomen","emphasis":true},{"text":" names the area between the chest and pelvis; "},{"text":"belly","emphasis":true},{"text":" is a familiar word for that area. "},{"text":"Stomach","emphasis":true},{"text":" names an internal organ, but people also use it in everyday reports such as “My stomach hurts.” The "},{"text":"waist","emphasis":true},{"text":" is the area around the body's middle; the "},{"text":"navel / belly button","emphasis":true},{"text":" is the small central mark on the abdomen. "},{"text":"Heart, lungs, liver, and kidneys","emphasis":true},{"text":" are internal organs. "},{"text":"Bone","emphasis":true},{"text":" is the hard material forming the skeleton."}],"span":[12,12],"phraseIds":["ch80-p274075644800616","ch80-p166237631084773","ch80-p11657656790957","ch80-p262691981949895","ch80-p199877435205056","ch80-p20343594774570","ch80-p27802155059262"]},{"id":"ch80-b3","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Clinical body words are useful even when a concern feels private. "},{"text":"Breast","emphasis":true},{"text":" names body tissue on the upper front of the torso; "},{"text":"nipple","emphasis":true},{"text":" is the small projecting part on a breast. "},{"text":"Groin","emphasis":true},{"text":" is the area where the lower abdomen meets the upper thigh. "},{"text":"Penis","emphasis":true},{"text":" is an external genital organ. "},{"text":"Vagina","emphasis":true},{"text":" names an internal genital passage; "},{"text":"vulva","emphasis":true},{"text":" names the external genital area around the vaginal opening. These are anatomical terms, not diagnoses or insults."}],"span":[14,14],"phraseIds":["ch80-p277220104886179","ch80-p232075708448267","ch80-p163209933626227","ch80-p153705572067702","ch80-p106725900547451","ch80-p108461057719652"]}],"line":8,"ja":"","theme":"health-vocabulary"},{"id":"80-study-2","title":"Symptoms and injuries","blocks":[{"id":"ch80-b4","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"A "},{"text":"symptom","emphasis":true},{"text":" is something experienced or noticed that may relate to a health problem."}],"span":[18,18],"phraseIds":["ch80-p239212796119172"]},{"id":"ch80-b5","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"Sore / painful:","emphasis":true},{"text":" hurting. "},{"text":"Itchy:","emphasis":true},{"text":" making you want to scratch."}],"phraseIds":[]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"Cough:","emphasis":true},{"text":" expelling air from the lungs; "},{"text":"runny nose:","emphasis":true},{"text":" fluid coming from the nose; "},{"text":"sore throat:","emphasis":true},{"text":" pain in the throat."}],"phraseIds":[]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"Fever:","emphasis":true},{"text":" an abnormally high body temperature; "},{"text":"headache / earache:","emphasis":true},{"text":" pain in the head or ear."}],"phraseIds":[]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"Nausea:","emphasis":true},{"text":" feeling that you may vomit; "},{"text":"vomiting / throwing up:","emphasis":true},{"text":" bringing stomach contents up; "},{"text":"diarrhea:","emphasis":true},{"text":" loose or watery bowel movements."}],"phraseIds":[]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"Rash:","emphasis":true},{"text":" an area of changed or irritated skin; "},{"text":"bruise:","emphasis":true},{"text":" discoloration from bleeding beneath the skin; "},{"text":"cut / scrape:","emphasis":true},{"text":" types of skin injury."}],"phraseIds":[]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"Burn, bite, cramp, sprain, broken bone:","emphasis":true},{"text":" different problems. A "},{"text":"sprain","emphasis":true},{"text":" involves an injured ligament; a "},{"text":"broken bone","emphasis":true},{"text":" is a fracture. Naming a possibility does not confirm it."}],"phraseIds":["ch80-p134435811743451","ch80-p257666337233754"]}],"span":[20,25],"phraseIds":["ch80-p134435811743451","ch80-p257666337233754"]},{"id":"ch80-b6","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Virus","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"infection","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"allergy","emphasis":true},{"text":", and "},{"text":"food poisoning","emphasis":true},{"text":" name possible causes or conditions, not interchangeable symptoms. You can say “I don't know what's causing it.”"}],"span":[27,27],"phraseIds":["ch80-p63410562199827","ch80-p47469063427125","ch80-p156997469027691","ch80-p12647717125158"]}],"line":16,"ja":"","theme":"health-vocabulary"},{"id":"80-study-3","title":"People and care words","blocks":[{"id":"ch80-b7","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"A "},{"text":"doctor","emphasis":true},{"text":" assesses and treats health concerns; a "},{"text":"nurse","emphasis":true},{"text":" helps care for patients and monitors their condition; a "},{"text":"pharmacist","emphasis":true},{"text":" works with medicines; a "},{"text":"dentist","emphasis":true},{"text":" works with teeth and oral health. A "},{"text":"surgeon","emphasis":true},{"text":" performs surgery; an "},{"text":"anesthesiologist","emphasis":true},{"text":" is a doctor specializing in anesthesia; a "},{"text":"paramedic","emphasis":true},{"text":" provides emergency medical care. A "},{"text":"pediatrician","emphasis":true},{"text":" specializes in children's medical care; a "},{"text":"midwife","emphasis":true},{"text":" provides care connected with pregnancy and birth; a "},{"text":"physical therapist","emphasis":true},{"text":" works on movement and physical function. An "},{"text":"optician","emphasis":true},{"text":" fits or supplies eyewear; a "},{"text":"therapist","emphasis":true},{"text":" needs context to identify the kind of therapy."}],"span":[31,31],"phraseIds":["ch80-p66417375051681","ch80-p94612825057173","ch80-p144569107289718","ch80-p29952656303500","ch80-p167390144000292","ch80-p100168243906722","ch80-p142532411374590","ch80-p158416337386914","ch80-p73501915170840","ch80-p132072687851236","ch80-p73573309181752","ch80-p3108594054087"]},{"id":"ch80-b8","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Emergency department / ER","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"ambulance","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"blood pressure","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"pulse / heart rate","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"blood test","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"X-ray","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"scan","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"checkup","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"bandage","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"stitches","emphasis":true},{"text":", "},{"text":"injection / shot","emphasis":true},{"text":", and "},{"text":"medication","emphasis":true},{"text":" are useful care terms. "},{"text":"Antibiotics","emphasis":true},{"text":" are a type of medicine, not a general word for every treatment."}],"span":[33,33],"phraseIds":["ch80-p122211163866742","ch80-p89890576728996","ch80-p14791442987183","ch80-p76229131085054","ch80-p273080008038190","ch80-p205735417881663","ch80-p53457264294945","ch80-p46673685468200","ch80-p90723433633683","ch80-p155592171976484","ch80-p178203392819952","ch80-p128286873482511","ch80-p164537724027694"]}],"line":29,"ja":"","theme":"health-vocabulary"},{"id":"80-words","title":"Words & phrases","blocks":[{"id":"80-glossary","type":"vocabulary","phraseIds":["ch80-v0","ch80-v1","ch80-v2","ch80-v3"]}]}],"practice":[{"id":"80-practice-0","title":"Take your turn","blocks":[{"id":"ch80-b9","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Use three fictional reports: a sore throat since Monday; an itchy arm with a rash; pain in the groin that started today."}],"span":[37,37]},{"id":"ch80-b10","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"number":1,"runs":[{"text":"Select the body part, symptom, and time for one report. Say it without selecting a diagnosis."}],"id":"ch80-b10-0"},{"number":2,"runs":[{"text":"Choose the professional you would ask about a prescription question, then formulate the question."}],"id":"ch80-b10-1"},{"number":3,"runs":[{"text":"Explain the difference between a symptom you notice and a cause you only suspect. Alone, say your explanations; with a partner, exchange cases."}],"id":"ch80-b10-2"}],"span":[39,41]}],"line":37,"ja":"","theme":"health-vocabulary","answers":[{"id":"ch80-b11","type":"answer","runs":[{"text":"Possibilities:","emphasis":true},{"text":" “My arm is itchy, and there's a rash.” “Could a pharmacist explain this medicine's instructions?” “I have a sore throat; I don't know the cause.” Check that your vocabulary identifies the location and experience accurately. Detailed reporting and care conversations follow; this vocabulary page does not establish what treatment you need."}],"span":[43,43]}]}],"phrases":[{"id":"ch80-p2521486346","en":"head","section":"80-study-1","context":"Body parts","kind":"word","studyId":"ch80-p263324456941496"},{"id":"ch80-p2023147977","en":"ears","section":"80-study-1","context":"Body parts","kind":"word","studyId":"ch80-p263324456941496"},{"id":"ch80-p106540219","en":"neck","section":"80-study-1","context":"Body parts","kind":"word","studyId":"ch80-p263324456941496"},{"id":"ch80-p1956425081","en":"shoulders","section":"80-study-1","context":"Body parts","kind":"word","studyId":"ch80-p263324456941496"},{"id":"ch80-p407252221","en":"chest","section":"80-study-1","context":"Body parts","kind":"word","studyId":"ch80-p263324456941496"},{"id":"ch80-p3377680803","en":"back","section":"80-study-1","context":"Body parts","kind":"word","studyId":"ch80-p263324456941496"},{"id":"ch80-p463893811","en":"arms","section":"80-study-1","context":"Body parts","kind":"word","studyId":"ch80-p263324456941496"},{"id":"ch80-p1260836494","en":"hands","section":"80-study-1","context":"Body parts","kind":"word","studyId":"ch80-p263324456941496"},{"id":"ch80-p1174244262","en":"hips","section":"80-study-1","context":"Body parts","kind":"word","studyId":"ch80-p263324456941496"},{"id":"ch80-p2809227909","en":"legs","section":"80-study-1","context":"Body parts","kind":"word","studyId":"ch80-p263324456941496"},{"id":"ch80-p443244932","en":"knees","section":"80-study-1","context":"Body parts","kind":"word","studyId":"ch80-p263324